export const CARD_SPEC_GUIDE = "Post a card to the current conversation: a native Slack or Discord message with a header, fields, tables, charts and links. Use it for structured results such as tables, metrics, status and comparisons, not for ordinary conversation.\nIt returns once the host has posted the card. If the spec breaks a rule below, nothing is posted and the result lists every problem; fix them and call again.\n\nspec: { \"root\": \"<key>\", \"elements\": { \"<key>\": { \"type\": \"<component>\", \"props\": { ... }, \"children\": [\"<key>\", ...] } } }\n\nComponents:\n- Card: { title?: string, subtitle?: string, imageUrl?: string } - Root of a message. Title renders as the card header, subtitle as secondary text. [accepts children]\n- Section: {  } - Groups related elements. [accepts children]\n- Text: { content: string, style?: \"plain\" | \"bold\" | \"muted\" } - A paragraph of markdown text. Use muted for footnotes.\n- Fields: {  } - Grid of label and value pairs. Children are Field elements. [accepts children]\n- Field: { label: string, value: unknown } - One label and value pair inside Fields. Good for KPIs.\n- Table: { headers: Array<string>, rows: Array<Array<unknown>>, align?: Array<\"left\" | \"center\" | \"right\">, caption?: string } - Table for row data. Every row has one cell per header. Slack and Discord left-align every column, so align is ignored.\n- Chart: { title: string, chart: { type: \"pie\", segments: Array<{ label: string, value: number }> } | { type: \"bar\" | \"line\" | \"area\", categories: Array<string>, series: Array<{ name: string, values: Array<number> }>, xLabel?: string, yLabel?: string } } - Chart. pie for shares of a whole, bar, line or area for series over categories.\n- Divider: {  } - Separator between groups.\n- Image: { url: string, alt: string } - Image from a public https URL.\n- Actions: {  } - Row of LinkButton elements that open URLs. [accepts children]\n- LinkButton: { label: string, url: string } - Button that opens a URL.\n\nRules:\n- The root element MUST be a Card. Every other element is a descendant of it. To group items inside the message, use Section, not another Card.\n- Messages are static once posted. $state, $item, $index, $template, repeat and visible are resolved when the card is built, but there are no inputs, so do not use $bindState or $bindItem.\n- Pick components by the shape of the data: Fields for a few key numbers, Table for row data, Chart for a trend or a share of a whole, Actions for links.\n- For a Table backed by state, set rows to { \"$state\": \"/path\" } where the path holds an array of rows (arrays or objects with one value per header).\n- Text content uses markdown: **bold**, _italic_ and `code`. Do not use headings inside Text. Put a link in an Actions row as a LinkButton: Slack shows a [label](url) link inside Text as written.\n- Field elements MUST be children of a Fields element. LinkButton elements MUST be children of an Actions element.\n- Every series in a bar, line or area Chart has exactly one value per category, in category order.\n- Every element MUST include a \"children\" array. Leaf elements use \"children\": [].\n- Slack: at most 1 Table, 2 Charts and 10 Fields per Fields element, 100 rows including the header and 20 columns per Table, 20 categories, 12 series or segments, 20-character labels and a 50-character title per Chart, 50 blocks per card, 25 LinkButtons per Actions, and 3000 characters per Text., Discord: at most 4,000 characters of text, tables and charts included, and 40 components per card.\n\nfallbackText (required): the same content as plain text. Search, thread history, the mobile app and the terminal show it; Slack and Discord show the card.";
